{"claims":[{"claim_text":"By “equality,” the group means equal protection under the law, the prohibition of discrimination based on race, sex, ethnicity, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender expression, age, profession and ability status, equal representation in legislative bodies, full voting rights for citizens on the basis of one person, one vote, and the right of working people to organize collectively in unions.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"The group believes the abolition of the U.S. Senate is necessary for full voting rights for citizens on the basis of one person, one vote.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"These principles of liberty and equality are indispensable to the self-government of a free people.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Denial of liberty and equality renders a government a tyranny.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Authoritarians on the Left dismiss the foundation of democracy in liberty and equality as bourgeois.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"The group defends the foundation of democracy in liberty and equality as the product of hard-fought struggles waged by working people against the powerful and wealthy.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"The group identifies African-Americans and other people of color, women, and other popular forces as having waged and continuing to wage struggles for liberty and equality against the powerful and wealthy.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"The group believes in the democratization of the economy in service of the public good and the general welfare.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[4]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

```json
{"claims":[{"claim_text":"By “equality,” we mean equal protection under the law, the prohibition of discrimination based on race, sex, ethnicity, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender expression, age, profession and ability status as called for in DSA’s Constitution, Bylaws and Resolution 33 on harassment, equal representation in legislative bodies, full voting rights for citizens on the basis of one person, one vote, which means the abolition of the U.S. Senate, and the right of working people to organize collectively in unions.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"By “liberty,” we mean the freedom of expression, the press, conscience and association, as well as the due process of law.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"These principles of liberty and equality are indispensable to the self-government of a free people; denial of them renders a government a tyranny.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Authoritarians on the Left dismiss the foundation of democracy in liberty and equality as bourgeois, but democratic socialists defend it as the product of hard-fought struggles waged by working people, especially African-Americans and other people of color, women, and other popular forces, against the powerful and wealthy who seek to limit democracy.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[3]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```
